\subsection{\code{BaseRQqlineLayerProcessor$qq_x_range()}}{
  The x interval the chart drew, taken from the Q-Q pairs

The group's HIGH call is the \code{qqnorm()} or \code{qqplot()} this line sits
on, and its recorded first argument is a \emph{sample} rather than either
drawn coordinate. So the range is read off the pairs \code{stats} computes,
which is what the chart put on the x axis.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{BaseRQqlineLayerProcessor$qq_x_range(layer_info)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
